==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|slang|lang=en}} Common abbreviation for many/any unit having the [[SI]] [[prefix]] '''[[mega-]]''', such as '''[[megahertz]]'''
#: {{context|computing|lang=en}} - ''My new computer has over 500 megs of RAM.'' = [[megabyte]]
#: ''(radio) - "What frequency does Radio XYZ broadcast on ?" "105.7 meg" = [[megahertz]]
#: ''(heating) - "a 250 meg gas heater" = [[megajoule]]s

====Usage notes====
* This usage is mostly verbal. It is less often used in writing.''

